ar head instead of that thick, plugged-up pressure behind my eyes. Somewhere along the way, "stuffed up" stopped being a thing that happened to me and became <em>who I was.</em></p><p>If you know that feeling — really know it — then you already understand why I'm writing this.</p>                    </div></div></div>      </div>    </div>  </div></section>


