      <div class="container "><div class="content-box content-box--large content-box--text-left content-box--left text-container"><h3 class="heading h2">&quot;But what does it actually feel like?&quot;</h3><p>I have to address this, because it was <em>my</em> biggest fear too — and it's the number-one question I see from people on the fence.</p><p>You're picturing waterboarding. Drowning. Gagging. Salt water down your throat.</p><p>Here's the truth from someone who was genuinely scared of it: it's a gentle, warm, controlled stream — not a blast. The device manages the pressure so you don't have to. Most of the "horror stories" come from technique on a <em>manual</em> rinse, which is exactly the problem Naväge's powered suction is built to solve. Warm your water slightly, follow the simple steps, and that fear tends to evaporate the first time you actually do it. As one reviewer put it: <em>"I had fear at first, but once I did it, I felt fine."</em></p></div>
