      <div class="container "><div class="content-box content-box--large content-box--text-left content-box--left text-container"><h3 class="heading h2">One last thing, from me to you</h3><p>I almost didn't write this. It's a strangely personal thing, telling strangers about your nose.</p><p>But I kept thinking about that 2 a.m. version of me, sitting on the edge of the bed, ready to just accept feeling foggy and tired forever. If there's even one person out there in that exact spot tonight — please, don't give up before you've tried the one thing that finally worked for me.</p><p>You deserve to breathe. You deserve to sleep. You deserve to stop organizing your whole life around your sinuses.</p><p>I never thought I'd feel this way again. You can.</p><p><strong>— Diane</strong></p><p><em>P.S. — Tip from experience: warm your saline solution to body temperature before you use it. That one small thing is the difference between "weird and cold" and "ahhh." It made me a believer on day one.</em></p></div>
